ModernFlow
==========

This skill's diagram vocabulary — the shape-carries-meaning grammar, the
per-type layout contracts, the complexity budgets, and the "one accent per
figure" rule — is adapted from:

  diagram-design
  https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design
  Copyright (c) 2025 Cathryn Lavery
  Licensed under the MIT License

What was adapted:
  - Shape semantics (stadium = terminal, rectangle = step, diamond = decision,
    ring + hub = loop) and the rule that shape, not fill colour, carries type
  - Parametric layout contracts: explicit inputs -> deterministic geometry
  - Complexity budgets per figure (node / edge / accent caps)
  - The "editorial-paper" style profile's palette and type roles

What is new here:
  - The "soft-gradient" style profile (palette sampled from reference footage)
  - WCAG-AA corrections to both palettes (the upstream `soft` token fails AA)
  - The motion grammar: entrance/exit vocabulary, seam rules, the three gates
  - The three-tier output model (still PNG / self-playing HTML / narrated MP4)
  - All scripts (font subsetting, contrast gate, PNG render, keyframe emitter)

diagram-design is a reference, not a dependency. This skill does not vendor,
execute, or require any of its code.

Fonts referenced by this skill (Inter, Instrument Serif, Geist, Noto Sans SC,
Noto Serif SC) are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 by their
respective authors and are fetched at build time, not vendored here.


Bundled fonts
-------------

assets/fonts/*.woff2 are subsetted copies of Inter, Noto Sans SC, Noto Serif SC,
Instrument Serif, Geist and Geist Mono, redistributed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. Copyright notices and the full licence text travel with them in
assets/fonts/OFL.txt, which is what the licence requires.

They are committed rather than downloaded because the whole point of this skill
is that two machines render the same picture, and a font that is absent does not
raise an error — the browser substitutes whatever the local system has.
